Description: Visualization and analysis of multiplex immunofluorescence data.
    Provides univariate and bivariate Ripley's K, nearest-neighbour G, the pair
    correlation function, Dixon's segregation statistic, and a cell-cell
    interaction variable, together with a container ('mif') that keeps clinical,
    per-sample and single-cell spatial data alongside the measures derived from
    them. Complete spatial randomness can be estimated either by permutation,
    following Wilson et al. <doi:10.1101/2021.04.27.21256104>, or from a
    closed-form expression that avoids permutations entirely. Count-based measures
    agree with the 'spatstat' family to floating-point precision.
